<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pandolfo IV Malatesta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1475">1475</a>–<a href="/years/1534">1534</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Pandolfaccio · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malatesta-family">Malatesta family</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pandolfo IV Malatesta, nicknamed Pandolfaccio, was the last Malatesta lord of Rimini, ruling from 1482. Unpopular and weak, he was driven out by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-borgia">Cesare Borgia</a> in 1500 and in 1503 handed his rights to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. He briefly recovered Rimini in 1522 before it passed definitively to the Papal States.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pandolfo-iv-malatesta.jpg" alt="Pandolfo IV Malatesta" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Domenico Ghirlandaio · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rimini120.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1500 Cesare Borgia drove out <b>Pandolfo IV Malatesta</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/lordship-of-rimini">Lordship of Rimini</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Rimini, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=44.06,12.57&amp;year=1513" aria-label="Rimini on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4851 604 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Pandolfo IV Malatesta"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5301 874h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5301 874h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=44.06,12.57&amp;year=1513">What was here in 1513? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
